<div id="abe-column-block-04ade38b-c736-4579-b810-470521120987" class="abe-column-block" data-block-type="FancyBlockColumn" data-block-id="144090796" style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; display: inline-block; font-size: 16px; vertical-align: top;">
  <table width="100%" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" role="presentation" style="table-layout: fixed; overflow-wrap: break-word; word-wrap: break-word; text-align: left; -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; border-spacing: 0; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt;">
    <tr>
      <td class="abe-column-block-padding" id="abe-column-block-04ade38b-c736-4579-b810-470521120987-padding" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt; padding: 15px;">
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Beginning Monday morning, June 10</strong>, a lengthy traffic pattern change will begin on Cassady Avenue in the vicinity of E. 5<sup>th</sup> Ave for the City of Columbus to construct major roadway improvements along Cassady from Delmar Dr. to 7<sup>th</sup> Ave.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">Cassady at Delmar Dr. south of the railroad tracks to E. 5<sup>th</sup> Ave. will be restricted to one-way northbound traffic, and it will be restricted to one-way southbound traffic from just north of E. 7<sup>th</sup> Ave. to E. 5<sup>th</sup> Ave. Drivers should follow the posted detour signage to get around the Cassady restrictions:</p>
<ul style="margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 15px;">
<li style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin-top: 0px;">Eastbound 5<sup>th</sup> Ave traffic that wants to travel north on Cassady will be detoured to Stelzer Rd. to 17<sup>th</sup>, and then to Johnstown Rd. back to Cassady.</li>
<li style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px;">Eastbound 5<sup>th</sup> Ave traffic that wants to travel south on Cassady will be detoured to Stelzer Rd./James Rd. to E. Broad St. back to Cassady.</li>
<li style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px;">Westbound 5<sup>th</sup> traffic that wants to travel north on Cassady will be detoured to Nelson Rd./US 62 to Airport Dr. back to Cassady.</li>
<li style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin-bottom: 15px;">Westbound 5<sup>th</sup> traffic that wants to travel south on Cassady will be detoured to Nelson Rd./US 62 to E. Broad St. back to Cassady.</li>
</ul>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">Expect this traffic pattern and posted detours to be in place for at least the next year. Access to local businesses in the construction zone will be maintained.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">The Cassady Avenue Improvements Project will reconstruct the roadway to a 3-lane, curb and gutter section with additional turn lanes at the intersection at E. 5th Avenue. Sidewalk will be installed along the east side of Cassady and a shared-use path along the west side. Other improvements include traffic signal replacement, street lighting, street trees where feasible and storm sewer. The 12" water line between Avalon Place and E. 5th Avenue will be replaced with a new 12" line.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">E. 5th Avenue will also be reconstructed with additional turn lanes at the Cassady Avenue intersection. The sidewalk will be replaced along both sides and lighting and utility systems replaced/relocated as necessary. Other improvements include street lighting, street trees where feasible, and storm sewer. Additional water line improvements will be made between N. Dawson Avenue and Northview Avenue.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Estimated completion of all construction is late 2026.</strong></p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">Please share this project update with others in the community. Anyone who wants to receive these construction updates can use this<a href="https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/OHCCC/subscriber/topics?qsp=OHCCC_10" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; color: #1D5782;"> link</a> to provide your email address.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;"> </p>
